 -A && git commit -q -m \"Cycle 68: S3b-M4 delivered as claudeDev/D1_s3_loop15.vi (md5 1a11d92a, ExecState 1 warm+cold, computation_diff 0 with machine SR pairing); Pre-decided 147; retrospective-cycle68 disposed; NEXT = loop 1.2/1.7 split plan\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit cycle 68 changes"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":5,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":5,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":5,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":5}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":38,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 68 delivered S3b-M4: `claudeDev\\D1_s3_loop15.vi` (md5 `1a11d92aacabf7ec844d65b8af19f39f`) is the new bed. It reaches ExecState 1 both with the VI already in memory and on a cold reopen, and `computation_diff` against the S1 copy is 0 rows. That is a structural check plus a graph comparison; the VI has never been run.\n\n- **Design change on my call (Pre-decided 147):** loop 1.5 now fires on the rising edge of the existing schedule signal, through an uninitialised yes/no shift register, instead of comparing frame counters. The counter route was dropped because no indicator carries the frame counter and there is no way to create `Select` or `Not Equal?`. It differs from the original in three rare cases, written in plain words as OPEN 58:\n  - a 'Frame rate' of 1 gives one autofocus instead of one per frame;\n  - a re-run without reloading the VI can skip the first autofocus;\n  - if loop 1.5 falls more than one frame (~11 ms) behind, it skips that autofocus.\n- **Tool fix:** `tools/vigraph.py` now pairs shift registers from LabVIEW's own register list, not by equal TOP position. The one leftover `#48 VISA` row came from the old pairing; with the fix it is gone. For-loop registers still fall back to TOP pairing because LabVIEW won't read theirs (error 1055).\n- **Retrospective:** both of its faults come from the 2026-09-23 PI hard-limit incident:\n  - The unmeasured zero was already fixed before this cycle, and this cycle's session start ran the new reference move.\n  - `bgrun` reported `rc=0` over a motor rejection because its failure check doesn't recognise `REJECTED` or `NOT at target`. That fix is act 2 of the next cycle.\n- **NEXT (cycle 69):** first write a one-page split plan for loops 1.2 and 1.7, which no current plan covers. It also has to schedule moving the nine rotor call sites to `SetCommand_signed.vi` (Pre-decided 133). S4–S6 come after that.\n- **For the user, not a stop:** running `D1_s3_loop15.vi` for real would drive the motors directly rather than through `motor_gate.py`. That isn't allowed while the rig is assembled, so it needs the rig taken apart or you present.\n- **Not done:** `git commit` needs your approval, so this cycle's changes are uncommitted.\n- **Cost:** reviews this cycle cost $11.75, and there were 3 failed predictions.","ttft_ms":2159,"type":"result","duration_ms":6037345,"uuid":"3a64f2f7-e471-4797-b239-2fbfc7015ef4","ttft_stream_ms":2048,"time_to_request_ms":390,"first_content_frame_ms":2048,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
